# OVERHEAD PRESS

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Overhead Press is a bilateral upper-body compound exercise designed to develop vertical pushing strength through coordinated force production from the lower body, trunk and upper limbs.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the foundational exercises for improving upper-body strength, trunk stability and whole-body force transmission.

---

# Philosophy

The Overhead Press develops force while standing.

Unlike the Bench Press, force must travel through the entire kinetic chain before reaching the load.

CAS selects the Overhead Press when improving whole-body integration provides greater transfer than isolated upper-body strength.

